      "flagged": true,
      "answer": "**Objective:** Design a Drupal module or distribution to ship default configuration and content as a single unit to other sites.\n\nThe system to achieve this is called **Recipes**, available in Drupal 10.3 and later.\n\nTo use Recipes, you need to create a directory with a `recipe.yml` file declaring the configuration, content, and module/theme dependencies to apply.\n\nA simple example of a recipe.yml file might look like this:\n```yaml\nname: My Feature\nversion: 1.0\ndescription: My feature description\ndependencies:\n  - module: Drupal/core\n    version: \"10.3\"\nfeatures:\n  - feature: myFeature\n    enabled: true\ncontent:\n  - node: myNode\n    title: My Node Title\n    body: My node body\n```\nVersion notes: The above Recipes system is available in Drupal 10.3 and later. The information is based on the provided evidence and is subject to change based on new updates.",
